## 6. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

### 6.1 MANDATORY IMPLEMENTATIONS

| Layer | Requirement | Implementation |
|-------|-------------|----------------|
| **Auth** | Password policy | Min 8 chars, 1 upper, 1 lower, 1 number, 1 special |
| **Auth** | JWT security | 15-min access, 7-day refresh, httpOnly cookies |
| **Auth** | Rate limiting | 5 login attempts per 15 min per IP |
| **Auth** | Account lockout | 30 min after 5 failed attempts |
| **Input** | Validation | Joi/Yup on all endpoints, strict typing |
| **Input** | SQL Injection | Sequelize parameterized queries ONLY |
| **Input** | XSS Protection | Sanitize HTML, Content-Security-Policy headers |
| **File** | Upload security | Max 5MB, whitelist extensions (jpg,png,pdf), scan with ClamAV |
| **File** | Storage | S3 with private buckets, signed URLs |
| **API** | CORS | Whitelist specific origins only |
| **API** | HTTPS | Enforce TLS 1.2+, HSTS headers |
| **Data** | Encryption at rest | AES-256 for sensitive fields (payout details) |
| **Data** | PII handling | Mask phone/email in logs, GDPR-compliant deletion |
| **Payment** | PCI compliance | Never store card numbers; use tokenization |
| **Audit** | Logging | All admin actions, payment events, auth events |

